Retry the revert of the task state when the database is lost

The `reverts_task_state` decorator (nova/compute/manager.py) clears the
task state that nova-api set before it handed an operation to
nova-compute, once the operation has failed. The revert is a single write,
an RPC call to nova-conductor, which answers a lost database with an
`oslo_messaging.RemoteError` of exc_type DBConnectionError. When an
operation fails while the database is gone, the revert fails as well and
only logs "Failed to revert task state for instance". The server then
keeps the task state until nova-compute restarts: `_sync_power_states`
skips an instance with a pending task, and only `_init_instance` resumes a
powering-on or powering-off at service start. Until then nova-api answers
a start, a volume detach and an interface attach of the server with a
409, because their `check_instance_state` allows no task state.

The nightly random chaos run 42752982735 (#1652) hit this. dizzy started
server d0b6ff17-3aaf-4ea5-baa1-2739f9032ea0 at 05:08:59, and
s06-mariadb-pod-kill began at 05:09:00. `start_instance` failed in its
first step, `_notify_about_instance_usage`, whose lazy load of the flavor
went through nova-conductor, and the revert failed at 05:09:01. The server
stayed stopped with the task state powering-on until dizzy's teardown
deleted it at 05:28:48. In the 11 minutes after the last fault had been
lifted and had recovered, nova-api answered 99 starts, 95 volume detaches
and 51 interface attaches of that server with a 409. In the same run the
revert of a failed build met s08-mariadb-pod-failure at 05:14:07; that
server did no harm only because dizzy deleted it two minutes later, which
the API allows in any task state.

The revert now goes through `compute_utils.call_with_db_retries` from
patch 0003. It retries a RemoteError of exc_type DBConnectionError with
waits that stop growing at 16 seconds and add up to 254 seconds, and gives
every other error one attempt as before, InstanceNotFound included. Once
the write succeeds, the server keeps its vm_state with no task state, its
instance fault records the error of the operation, and the next action of
the API reaches nova-compute again. When the 254 seconds run out, the
revert logs its failure and the server keeps the task state, as it does
without the patch. The NOTE above `call_with_db_retries` names the new
caller.

Seven methods keep the single revert; `_REVERTS_TASK_STATE_ONCE` names
them. Six are RPC calls, not casts, so a caller waits for their answer:
nova-api for set_admin_password, nova-conductor for
reserve_block_device_name and for the four steps of a cross-cell resize. A
revert that waited would hold that caller as well, and the caller of
set_admin_password gives up after rpc_response_timeout. terminate_instance
already clears its task state in the retried write of its ERROR state
(patch 0003), so a second round of waits would only hold its RPC worker
twice as long. The other 26 wrapped methods retry: 23 RPC casts, among
them start_instance and stop_instance, `_do_build_and_run_instance`, which
runs in the build's own thread, `_snapshot_instance` and power_update.
snapshot_instance and backup_instance wrap `_snapshot_instance`, so a
database that stays away for longer than 254 seconds holds them for a
second round.

During an outage each failed operation holds the worker of nova-compute
that ran it until its revert succeeds or gives up: an RPC executor worker
for a cast. Once failed operations fill the pool
(executor_thread_pool_size, 64 by default), every other RPC to that
nova-compute queues behind them until the database is back, as patch 0003
describes for failed deletes. A worker frees within 16 seconds of the
database's return.

Tests: four new tests in nova/tests/unit/compute/test_compute_mgr.py fail
without the patch. test_start_instance_reverts_task_state_after_lost_database
replays the night: the start fails on a lost database, two reverts meet
it, and the third persists stopped with no task state.
test_start_instance_revert_gives_up_after_lost_database pins 19 writes,
waits of 254 seconds in all and the logged failure.
test_reverts_task_state_once_for_the_named_methods pins one attempt for
set_admin_password and 19 for any other method.
test_reverts_task_state_once_names_methods_of_the_manager walks the
decorators of every name in the set, so a rename upstream that leaves a
name wrapping nothing fails it. The upstream tests of the decorator,
test_reverts_task_state_instance_not_found and test_state_revert in
nova/tests/unit/compute/test_compute.py, revert on a reachable database
and pass unchanged, as do the three terminate tests of patch 0003.

Proof: tests/container-images/verify_nova.sh asserts in the built image
that the revert of a failed start persists on its third write after two
lost databases, and that set_admin_password still reverts once.

Applies to nova 33.0.0 (2026.1), on top of patch 0003, whose helper it
calls.

Upstream status: not yet proposed.

